# Ketramose: "can't attack ... unless there are seven or more cards in exile" (a card in any player's exile counts) and
# "Whenever one or more cards are put into exile from graveyards and/or the battlefield during your turn, you draw a card and lose
# 1 life." Bot2 discards an Island at the end of each of its turns 2-10 (five in its graveyard) and casts an Ornithopter on turn 12.
# Turn 13, Bot1: Soul-Guide Lantern's enters trigger exiles one Island (1 in exile; one trigger: Bot1 19), sacrificing it
# exiles the other four at once (5; ONE trigger for the four cards: Bot1 18), Swords to Plowshares exiles the Ornithopter from the
# battlefield (6; Bot1 17). With six cards in exile Ketramose is refused as an attacker (the Ornithopter of Bot1 is why
# the declaration is asked). Turn 15: Bot2's turn-14 discard is exiled by the second Lantern (7; Bot1 16) and Ketramose attacks
# unblocked: lifelink 4, Bot1 20, Bot2 16.

